{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011CfbbVCTZVFTjaQA5Td78t", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "**Banker's rounding** (also called round-half-to-even, or `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`) is a rule for values that fall exactly halfway between two candidates. Round to the nearest even digit instead of always rounding up.\n\n- 2.5 \u2192 2\n- 3.5 \u2192 4\n- 0.125 \u2192 0.12 (to 2 decimals)\n- 0.135 \u2192 0.14\n\nAnything that isn't exactly a tie rounds the usual way, so 2.4 \u2192 2 and 2.6 \u2192 3.\n\n**Why accountants like it**\n\n1. **It's unbiased.** The usual \"round half up\" rule always pushes ties in the same direction. Over thousands of line items, such as interest, tax, or currency conversions, that adds up to a systematic upward drift. With half-even, ties round up about as often as they round down, so the errors cancel out.\n2. **Totals stay closer to the truth.** The sum of rounded values tracks the sum of the unrounded values better. This matters for reconciliation, where a one-cent discrepancy across many rows is hard to chase down.\n3. **It's a standard.** It's the default in IEEE 754 floating point and in many financial systems and regulations. Using it means your numbers match other systems.\n\n**Caveats**\n\n- The bias reduction only applies to exact ties. With binary floats, 0.125 is exactly representable but 0.135 isn't, so use a decimal type (such as Python's `Decimal` or Java's `BigDecimal`) for money.\n- Some jurisdictions or contracts mandate half-up, so check which rule applies.\n- Python's built-in `round()` uses half-even, which surprises people expecting `round(2.5) == 3`.\n\nThe project memory also records that tax in this codebase uses `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. That's consistent with the above, though I haven't opened that memory or the code."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 7377, "cache_read_input_tokens": 11903, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 7377}, "output_tokens": 2, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "77ae57ca-290c-4141-9fbb-4fbbe8d29f68", "uuid": "16373261-849b-45d7-9ea2-f34224e39383", "timestamp": "2026-10-01T13:27:58.335Z", "request_id": "req_011CfbbVC5WA6dLes8qGtn7K"}
